1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,127
<i>Chief!</i>

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:04,504
<i>I'm so excited about this!</i>

3
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:07,007
<i>We're all excited here, Blaire.</i>

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:08,466
<i>So, I think we can start?</i>

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,260
<i>Okay.</i>

6
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:12,721
<i>So, Billy and I discussed it,</i>

7
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>and after everything that's happened,</i>

8
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:18,560
<i>we agreed that we need a fresh start.</i>

9
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:21,187
<i>We reviewed where we are today</i>

10
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,314
<i>and where we wanted to be.</i>

11
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:25,734
<i>So, first things first,</i>

12
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>we're not changing our name.</i>

13
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:30,572
<i>We're still LoveList.</i>

14
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,449
<i>Yay!</i>

15
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,868
<i>How's life treating you, Ma?</i>

16
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:37,120
<i>Are you eating well here?</i>

17
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>Don't worry about me.</i>

18
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:45,795
<i>I just want to apologize again for what</i>
<i>I did to your daughter and Precious.</i>

19
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>Mariela.</i>

20
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:52,343
<i>Little by little,</i>
<i>I'll make it up to you too.</i>

21
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:57,098
<i>It's enough for me</i>
<i>that both of you are on good terms now.</i>

22
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,435
<i>Take care of each other, okay?</i>

23
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:03,730
<i>And you? Are you doing well?</i>

24
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:06,399
<i>I'm doing great, Ma.</i>

25
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,194
<i>Billy helped me out</i>
<i>with some startup capital,</i>

26
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:12,655
<i>and now we're business partners</i>
<i>in an internet cafe.</i>

27
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:13,865
[MARIELA]
<i>Really?</i>

28
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>Come on!</i>

29
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:18,536
<i>Yes, I understand, LoveLister Joanne.</i>

30
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,580
<i>Healing takes time.</i>

31
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:23,500
<i>Forgiveness isn't instant,</i>

32
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:27,545
<i>even if you've accepted the apology</i>
<i>of the person who hurt you.</i>

33
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:38,056
<i>I bought these with my first paycheck,</i>

34
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:41,184
<i>from our very first earnings</i>
<i>from the internet cafe.</i>

35
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,604
<i>If you're still hurt,</i>

36
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:48,191
<i>or if every now and then,</i>

37
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:51,986
<i>you're still affected</i>
<i>by the history of betrayal,</i>

38
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,571
<i>that's normal.</i>

39
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:58,284
<i>But it doesn't make you</i>
<i>a bad person, okay?</i>

40
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:02,580
<i>It just means that the healing</i>

41
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:05,834
<i>is still happening.</i>

42
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,920
<i>Healing should never be rushed.</i>

43
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:12,841
<i>- Dad, I packed you some food.</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Mm!</i>

44
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,467
<i>- How tasty.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

45
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:17,971
- [BEA] <i>That'll be mine instead.</i>
<i>- Right. That's your favorite.</i>

46
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:19,597
<i>- Oh, she'll eat it all.</i>
- [BEA] <i>Okay.</i>

47
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,393
<i>- Bye-bye, Pa!</i>
<i>- Bye-bye.</i>

48
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:24,769
<i>Extension?</i>

49
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,688
<i>Extension? You've made us</i>
<i>extend a lot already.</i>

50
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:27,772
<i>I know, right?</i>

51
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:28,940
<i>- But, Bea…</i>
<i>- Mm?</i>

52
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:32,318
<i>I hope you and Papa</i>
<i>will visit us more often.</i>

53
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,196
<i>Of course! Won't I be the one</i>
<i>to take you home from the…</i>

54
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,198
[OLIVER AND BEA]
<i>Internet cafe!</i>

55
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:39,325
<i>- Bye-bye.</i>
<i>- Mm!</i>

56
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,910
<i>Okay.</i>

57
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:50,837
AMIHAN HOME

58
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:56,676
Grandpa.

59
00:02:57,260 --> 00:03:01,598
Would you like to hear Mom's song again?

60
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,227
Do you still remember it?

61
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,524
[JORDAN] It's about home.

62
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,403
Home is where the heart is.

63
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:28,374
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

64
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:33,171
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

65
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:38,468
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

66
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:43,973
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

67
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:46,726
<i>♪ Oh baby ♪</i>

68
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:51,439
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

69
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:56,486
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

70
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:59,822
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you ♪</i>

71
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:02,033
<i>♪ Everything changed? ♪</i>

72
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,827
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

73
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:09,207
<i>♪ Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

74
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:13,378
[JUDE BREATHES DEEPLY]

75
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:19,676
[JUDE BREATHING HEAVILY]

76
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,761
I want to go home too.

77
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:24,722
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:25,890
My grandson.

79
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:34,691
T-Take me home.

80
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,404
Okay, Grandpa. [SNIFFLES]

81
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:45,576
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:05,972
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

83
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:24,157
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:30,598
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:34,644
[RAIN PATTERING]

86
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:56,415
- [EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [RAIN CONTINUES PATTERING]

87
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,362
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [TRAFFIC NOISE]

88
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:29,365
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

89
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:31,576
I'm sorry I'm late.

90
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:33,161
- I'm super late. I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

91
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:35,079
- Take a seat. Want a beer?
- Traffic was so heavy.

92
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,497
- Yes, please.
- [BILLY] Okay.

93
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,332
- It's his first time.
- How's the drinks?

94
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:39,584
Good.

95
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,169
- Boss.
- Boss.

96
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,753
- [JORDAN] Two beers.
- Two beers.

97
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,630
- I got you, boss.
- Uh, here it is.

98
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:46,716
Look, guys. He's getting me drunk.

99
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:48,092
You're getting me drunk.

100
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:49,802
- Here, boss.
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

101
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:52,388
- [JORDAN] Thank you, guys.
- You're welcome, boss.

102
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,598
[VALERIE] Cheers.

103
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:58,769
- Hey!
- Hey.

104
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:00,813
Didn't you just get promoted to manager?

105
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:03,900
Why not try catching feelings
with someone else?

106
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:06,652
- With whom?
- Robbie, my love!

107
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:10,156
Get me drunk.

108
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:11,782
Sure, come on.

109
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:13,910
- Here, here, here.
- [BLAIRE] Robbie!

110
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,289
- [BONG CHUCKLES]
- Go home once you finish that.

111
00:08:18,372 --> 00:08:19,582
[BLAIRE] Aw!

112
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,919
- [WOMAN] Right, baby?
- [VALERIE] Um…

113
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:24,837
[VALERIE] Especially, you know…

114
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:27,256
It's more expensive, so like…

115
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:34,096
Oh?

116
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,099
It's easy for you to say that
because you're happy.

117
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,185
- Of course.
- You're happy.

118
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,064
Hey, the baby kicked!

119
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,566
- Baby!
- [GUSHING]

120
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,151
- I'm the favorite godmother.
- Maybe!

121
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,819
Of course. Of course, babe.

122
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,279
- So cute!
- [CHUCKLES]

123
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,618
More?

124
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:59,872
You know, I'm sure
they're both proud of you.

125
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:03,709
Mm! That's what they told me.

126
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,546
Look.

127
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:11,175
You got everything you wanted.

128
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:17,682
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,101
Not quite yet.

130
00:09:20,184 --> 00:09:24,647
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:30,695
[JORDAN CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

132
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:37,785
Grandpa Jude, did you just hear him?

133
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,495
- He's being stubborn.
- Sorry, Grandpa.

134
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,080
I can't help it. She's beautiful.

135
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:43,708
Grandpa, he really won't stop.

136
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:44,709
Stop it, please.

137
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:48,629
Cheers, guys! Let's go!

138
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:52,091
- Yay!
- Come on!

139
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:53,759
Celebration!

140
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,094
Cheers!

141
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:56,220
Let's go, guys!

142
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,847
- Cheers!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

143
00:09:57,930 --> 00:10:01,058
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

144
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,185
- [BLAIRE] Cheers!
- I can still smell it.

145
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,729
- [BLAIRE] Congrats!
- [MAN] Yes!

146
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:07,815
- [WOMAN] Congratulations!
- Thank you.

147
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:10,192
[ALL CHUCKLING]

148
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:14,238
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING, THEN FADES]

149
00:10:16,782 --> 00:10:18,784
As a painter,

150
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:21,704
I always look for the perfect colors,

151
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,624
perfect lighting,

152
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,167
and perfect composition.

153
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:28,252
And at some point,

154
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:32,923
I looked for the perfect relationship.

155
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:36,469
And what I learned from Toni

156
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:43,267
is that our relationship isn't
and will never be perfect.

157
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:44,810
Our love story will never be perfect.

158
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:47,980
There'll be misunderstandings,

159
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:50,691
caused by me, of course,

160
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:55,237
and there'll be ups and downs.

161
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,947
But thank you, Toni.

162
00:10:57,031 --> 00:11:00,159
Thank you for always forgiving me,

163
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:03,204
and for the endless
second chances you give me

164
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:04,914
to be a better person.

165
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:07,833
[YANI INHALES DEEPLY]

166
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:10,461
There's another thing I learned.

167
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:12,671
When you love someone,

168
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:15,299
don't hide your feelings.

169
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:17,134
Don't wait another day to tell them.

170
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:21,347
Let the world know how you feel.

171
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,809
Love is like a canvas.

172
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:30,022
If you're scared to make
your first brushstroke,

173
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,608
you won't be able to create anything.

174
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:38,489
When you're sure about that person,
don't be afraid. [CHUCKLES]

175
00:11:38,572 --> 00:11:39,865
Go for it.

176
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,452
Toni,

177
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,663
I love you so much.

178
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:49,417
And I'm going to tell
the whole world about it.

179
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,293
[GUESTS CHUCKLE]

180
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:53,462
Now,

181
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:55,381
every day, and forever.

182
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:58,759
[APPLAUSE]

183
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,469
- Whoo!
- Whoo!

184
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:02,805
Let's go! Yeah!

185
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:03,848
- [GUEST CHUCKLING]
- Yes!

186
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,850
- Go, Toni!
- Finally!

187
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:09,270
- [APPLAUSE, CHEERING]
- Go, Yani!

188
00:12:09,353 --> 00:12:15,693
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:37,923
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,117
What's this drama?

191
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:07,036
You're so serious!

192
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:10,247
You should be happy! Look.

193
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:14,627
The comments are great,
all because of your suggestion.

194
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:16,170
Very good!

195
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:19,507
It's great! It's so nice, dude.

196
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:23,719
LoveList, your best friend in love.

197
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:26,388
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm!

198
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:36,398
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:37,525
[BILLY GRUNTS]

200
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,408
Do you remember?

201
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:50,829
Toni and Yani were the first couple
to match on LoveList.

202
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:52,665
It's amazing.

203
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:57,294
Yani checked all of Toni's boxes.

204
00:13:58,003 --> 00:14:00,839
But it's not really that simple, is it?

205
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:03,842
Because even though
they were a perfect match,

206
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:07,096
even though they seemed
destined for each other,

207
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:10,057
they still went through a lot.

208
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:14,520
You know how they are
when they fight. My God!

209
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:20,401
It's like destiny said,
"There, I brought you together."

210
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,487
"Now, it's your turn."

211
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:28,200
"It's your turn to write your love story."

212
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:33,455
So, dude, I thought…

213
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:37,918
What if we upgrade
our features on LoveLine?

214
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:41,755
We could include counseling for couples.

215
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,049
Only if it's okay with you.
What do you think?

216
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,011
Hello?

217
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:48,929
Hello?

218
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,932
Hello, Jordan? Are you here?

219
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:55,185
If you're here,
make your presence known, please.

220
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,730
[BOTH CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

221
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,609
Be careful what you wish for.

222
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:04,820
If I make you feel my presence again,

223
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,405
I might not take it back anymore.

224
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:10,409
Hm? Are you sure?

225
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:13,913
I'm making my presence known.

226
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,332
No! [GIGGLES]

227
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:17,499
You're crazy.

228
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:22,004
I've been talking for a while,
but you're just being quiet.

229
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:26,175
I'll miss this.

230
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:29,136
There's nothing like this in Australia.

231
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:31,472
Huh?

232
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:39,855
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,565
Dude.

234
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,360
- My friends in Australia…
- Okay.

235
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:48,030
They want me to build
a Jade & Jude's in Sydney.

236
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:52,117
They'll take care of the funding.
I'll be the industrial partner.

237
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:55,412
But I have to stay there.

238
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:59,541
You know, to help manage the bar

239
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,919
and scout for performers.

240
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:04,338
They also want me to sing.

241
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:06,840
Wow.

242
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,594
That's good news, right?

243
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:13,889
That's okay, dude! Congratulations!

244
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:19,436
Why is your face like that? Jordan.

245
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:22,272
What's on your mind?

246
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:25,776
Robbie can handle the Jade & Jude's here.

247
00:16:25,859 --> 00:16:27,236
- I know that.
- Okay.

248
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:30,614
If it's LoveList, then fine.

249
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,158
File your leave, and I'll approve it.

250
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:35,285
[HESITATES] Billy.

251
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:38,580
This is long-term.

252
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,583
I could be gone for…

253
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:45,212
I don't know, a year? At least?

254
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:51,135
- A year?
- At least.

255
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,223
But I haven't--

256
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:00,144
I haven't made a decision yet.

257
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,316
Oh.

258
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,528
So, it's like…

259
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,575
when you studied in Australia, right?

260
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:17,619
And then you'll come back, won't you?

261
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,496
You can take a vacation here.

262
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:22,082
I'm not sure when that will be.

263
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:26,128
I have to focus.

264
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:30,007
My friends will invest
a lot of money in this.

265
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:32,926
I don't want it to go to waste.

266
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,428
[JORDAN INHALES DEEPLY]

267
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:36,180
I can't have distractions.

268
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:37,556
Okay.

269
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:43,395
But after a year,
maybe you'll be done focusing.

270
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:46,065
Then you'll come back.

271
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:50,235
Two years?

272
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,949
I'm sure you'll be done focusing by then.

273
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:58,994
You can come back here.

274
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:01,538
It's not that easy to focus.

275
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:06,335
Look, I--

276
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:11,131
I think I just need to be away.

277
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,888
So, how long?

278
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:20,849
It might be for good.

279
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:26,105
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

280
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,606
I just thought…

281
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,776
A lot of things happened.

282
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:33,737
So…

283
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:37,157
if I really want to move on…

284
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:43,455
I have to start over.

285
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,920
Hmm.

286
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:52,172
Okay.

287
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:57,928
So you might not come back.

288
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,147
It's okay.

289
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:10,232
Imagine!

290
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:15,112
You'll make Grandpa Jude's name
and your mom's name known

291
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,613
to another country.

292
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,907
You even get to sing!

293
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,160
More women will definitely approach you.

294
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:22,828
They'll go crazy over you.

295
00:19:22,911 --> 00:19:26,248
And then you can write
all the songs you want!

296
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:28,667
You might forget about us.

297
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:34,214
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

298
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:56,111
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:16,715
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,058
<i>I think I just need to be away.</i>

301
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,686
<i>So, how long?</i>

302
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,480
<i>It might be for good.</i>

303
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:43,659
<i>If I really want to move on…</i>

304
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,998
<i>I have to start over.</i>

305
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:57,089
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:27,995
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:21:39,923 --> 00:21:41,049
<i>What do you think?</i>

308
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:42,926
<i>Mom.</i>

309
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:44,803
<i>Grandpa.</i>

310
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:46,596
<i>Should I push through with this?</i>

311
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:48,682
<i>I can leave.</i>

312
00:21:49,766 --> 00:21:51,768
<i>I don't have any family left here,</i>

313
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:53,312
<i>except Billy.</i>

314
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:54,938
<i>But what if…</i>

315
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,149
<i>What if I told her</i>

316
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:00,360
<i>that I still love her?</i>

317
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:12,164
<i>- Banana split!</i>
<i>- Banana split!</i>

318
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,540
<i>- Oh!</i>
- [LAUGHING]

319
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:14,958
<i>Hey, don't laugh at me!</i>

320
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:17,586
<i>- Huh?</i> [GRUNTS]
- [LAUGHING]

321
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:19,212
[GIGGLES]

322
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:21,548
- [GIRL] <i>You lose! You lose!</i>
- [BOY] <i>Don't rub it in my face!</i>

323
00:22:21,631 --> 00:22:23,258
- [GIRL] <i>Whoa!</i>
- [BOY] <i>Okay.</i>

324
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:31,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]
